      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Digestive System – Meaning and Need"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Digestion begins in the mouth where salivary amylase breaks down complex carbohydrates.",
        "The stomach secretes gastric juices, including pepsin and HCl, to process proteins in an acidic environment.",
        "The liver secretes bile which emulsifies lipids for efficient enzyme action.",
        "The small intestine serves as the primary organ for final enzymatic digestion and nutrient absorption.",
        "The large intestine reabsorbs water and electrolytes, preparing unabsorbed waste for elimination."
      ],
      "id": "u3gtiaj"
    },
