    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Bile juice is stored in the gallbladder and contains no digestive enzymes, yet it is crucial for fat emulsification.",
        "Hydrochloric acid (HCl) in the stomach creates the acidic pH necessary to convert inactive pepsinogen into active pepsin.",
